1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
 When it comes to data entry, there are several different methods that can be used to input information into a computer or database.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
 In this lecture, we are going to take a closer look at some of the most common types of data entry and their uses.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
 The first type of data entry is manual data entry.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:27,000
 This is the process of manually typing information into a computer or database using a keyboard or other input device.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,000
 Manual data entry is used often for small amounts of data or for situations where the data is easily captured through other means.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
 Another common type of data entry is automated data entry through scanning.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:50,000
 This process involves using a scanner to capture an image of a document and then using software to automatically extract the data from that image.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
 This method is used for large amounts of data or for situations where the data is already in a physical format such as paper documents.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
 Another type of data entry is barcode scanning.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:12,000
 This process involves using a barcode scanner to read a barcode on an item and then using that information to automatically input data into a computer or database.

11
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
 This method is often used in retail or manufacturing environments to track inventory or other information.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
 In recent years, mobile data entry has become increasingly popular.

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,000
 This process allows it to be entered remotely using a mobile device such as a smartphone or tablet.

14
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:39,000
 This is particularly used in situation where the data is being collected out in the field such as during a survey and inspection.

15
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,000
 Finally, we have voice recognition data entry.

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:49,000
 This method of data entry involves using voice recognition software to convert spoken word into text.

17
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
 This is useful in situations where the data is being entered quickly such as during a telephone call.

18
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
 These are just a few of the most common types of data entry.

19
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:08,000
 Each has its own advantages and disadvantages and the best method will depend on the specific situation and the type of data being collected.

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:19,000
 Whether you are working in health care, finance, retail or any other field, understanding the different types of data entry are essential for success.

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:26,000
 Thank you for watching. We hope you have a better understanding of the different types of data entry and how they can use it.

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
 If you are interested in learning more, be sure to check out our full course on data entry.

